  "summary": "Security-research / proof-of-concept package: alloy-graphql (npm)",
  "details": "The package's preinstall hook runs index.js, which collects system information from the install machine — hostname, username, home directory, DNS servers, the full package.json, and the contents of /etc/passwd and /etc/hosts — and POSTs it as JSON to the remote host ipbtwv9063nc5hvhodh0s4u9x03rrhf6[.]oastify[.]com on port 443. The exfiltrated data includes the /etc/passwd file, exposing system account information. The exfiltration occurs automatically at install time.",
